{"seq":17,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T14:22:28.050Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7cad1fdaf31a1311ce3dddf305df2045c14f765572aa1a2a838ac2aa46187223","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared digests. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#4419*: from *Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)* (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was then escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n• *#PD-4492*: from *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (5 Oct 2025, teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct.\n\nMoss's other QFL notes (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers. The Central notes have #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those belong to Central accounts, not QFL.\n\nBefore this goes in the weekly notes, one thing to check: Marcus's own note (Q2 expansion wrap, 14 Jul 2025) also lists *#4419*, but describes it as Gate 3 BOL printer lag, not scanners. Either one ticket number covers two different issues or one of the notes has it wrong."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
